From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 +0000
From: noname <noname@example.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 22:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0001 keep the sign-in card and its primary button out of
 the layer path

The released v1.0.4 starts on the seat and dies by itself about fifteen
seconds into the sign-in flow, twice in a row, with nothing in its own log:

  Nov 09 20:48:46 systemd-coredump[851208]: Process 850866 (opennow-qt)
  of user 1000 terminated abnormally without generating a coredump
  Nov 09 20:50:55 systemd-coredump[851343]: Process 851343 (opennow-qt) ...

The same binary stopped under gdb -batch -ex run -ex bt answers on thread 18
"QSGRenderThread", SIGSEGV inside the driver, and the frames under it name
the pass that renders a QML layer into a texture:

  #0 0x0000ffffd96764c8 in ?? () from /vendor/lib/libvulkan_VSI.so.1.3.3
  #4 QSGBatchRenderer::Renderer::renderMergedBatch(...) from libQt6Quick.so.6
  #5 QSGBatchRenderer::Renderer::recordRenderPass(...)
  #6 QSGBatchRenderer::Renderer::render()
  #7 QSGRenderer::renderScene()
  #8 QSGRhiLayer::grab()
  #9 QSGRhiLayer::updateTexture()
  #10 QSGRenderer::preprocess()

So the death is QSGRhiLayer, not the video path: there is no video here,
the launch has not selected a game yet, and the only things on the login
path that ask Qt6Quick for a layer at this pin are DesktopSignInScreen.qml,
the primary action button through layer.enabled: action.primary and the
sign-in card itself through layer.enabled: true, both with a MultiEffect
drop shadow. The rest of the layer uses at bec4a0b sit in the home screen,
the store hero and the stream screen, and none of those draw before the
account record is written.

Draw the card and the button directly, which keeps the login path off the
driver path that segfaults. This is the whole patch series OpenNOW carries
on this board: it only creates the account record that OpenNOWLite reads
back over the core RPC, and the picture, the decoder, the audio and the
seat keyboard all belong to opennowlite, so no streaming patch comes back.

---
diff --git a/opennow-qt/qml/desktop/auth/DesktopSignInScreen.qml b/opennow-qt/qml/desktop/auth/DesktopSignInScreen.qml
index f3bb04e5..961f1d8d 100644
--- a/opennow-qt/qml/desktop/auth/DesktopSignInScreen.qml
+++ b/opennow-qt/qml/desktop/auth/DesktopSignInScreen.qml
@@ -111,14 +111,8 @@ FocusScope {
             border.width: action.activeFocus ? 2 : action.primary || action.quiet ? 0 : 1
             border.color: action.activeFocus ? DesktopTokens.focus : root.cardSeam
             opacity: action.enabled ? 1 : 0.5
-            layer.enabled: action.primary
-            layer.effect: MultiEffect {
-                shadowEnabled: true
-                shadowColor: "#2E6EE7B7"
-                shadowBlur: 0.6
-                shadowVerticalOffset: DesktopTokens.px(8)
-                shadowHorizontalOffset: 0
-            }
+            // Drawn directly: the layered shadow below crashed the Vulkan
+            // driver on the STM32MP257F, see the sign-in card.
         }
     }
 
@@ -251,14 +245,11 @@ FocusScope {
                 color: Theme.lightMode ? Qt.rgba(Theme.shell.r, Theme.shell.g, Theme.shell.b, 0.92) : "#D10B0F1A"
                 border.width: 1
                 border.color: root.cardSeam
-                layer.enabled: true
-                layer.effect: MultiEffect {
-                    shadowEnabled: true
-                    shadowColor: "#8C000000"
-                    shadowBlur: 1
-                    shadowVerticalOffset: DesktopTokens.px(24)
-                    shadowHorizontalOffset: 0
-                }
+                // The card used to be a QML layer with a MultiEffect drop
+                // shadow. On the STM32MP257F the VeriSilicon Vulkan driver
+                // segfaults in QSGRhiLayer::grab() when the card re-renders
+                // while the QR panel appears, so it is drawn directly now. The
+                // button above lost its layer for the same reason.
 
                 Column {
                     id: cardColumn
